Yes—that handles template sources cleanly without adding `track = true`:

```toml
[dotfiles]
"~/templates/**" = { mode = "track" }
"~/.zshrc" = { mode = "track" }

"~/.gitconfig" = {
  mode = "template",
  source = "~/templates/gitconfig.tera",
}
```

This tracks the templates and `.zshrc`, but **not** the generated `.gitconfig`. Referencing a source doesn’t enroll it; the explicit tracking declaration does.

I’ll keep `mode = "track"`. The revision needs to add glob enrollment—including newly created matching files—and allow tracking declarations to overlap managed destinations without treating that as a deployment conflict. Tracking a directory directly will also include its descendants, so `~/templates` works without `/**`.

